        Welcome to South Eastern Arabic College
    </h2>

    <!-- Main Content -->
    <p>
        <strong>South Eastern Arabic College is a distinguished institution dedicated to excellence in the teaching
            of the Arabic language, Qur’anic sciences, Hadith, and Islamic studies. Firmly rooted in Islamic faith
            and a rich scholarly tradition, the college harmoniously integrates classical learning with modern
            academic methodologies and internationally recognized educational standards.</strong>
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>Our educational philosophy is holistic in nature. Beyond academic achievement, we place strong
            emphasis on character development, discipline, leadership, and the cultivation of sound moral values. We
            believe that true education nurtures both the intellect and the character, preparing learners to serve
            society with knowledge, integrity, and responsibility.</strong>
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>Education at South Eastern Arabic College is inclusive and accessible. Learning begins from the age
            of five, and students of all ages are warmly welcomed. There are no rigid restrictions on prior
            qualifications, as we believe that the pursuit of knowledge should remain open to all who seek it. While
            the college primarily serves the Muslim community, learners from all backgrounds are encouraged to join,
            reflecting our commitment to mutual respect, ethical learning, and social harmony. Knowledge, in our
            view, is a
            universal trust meant to benefit humanity as a whole.</strong>
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>The college offers a unique academic pathway for students who wish to pursue Islamic scholarship
            alongside their mainstream education. Learners are able to continue their formal schooling while
            receiving structured and systematic training toward becoming qualified Moulavi or
        </strong><strong>Moulavia</strong><strong>. In addition, guidance is provided for those seeking to further
            their studies through degree programs at recognized Islamic universities abroad.</strong>
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>At the same time, students are strongly encouraged and supported to obtain degrees from universities
            in Sri Lanka and to pursue professional qualifications in fields such as medicine, engineering, law,
            education, and other specialized disciplines. This balanced approach ensures that graduates are
            well-equipped for both religious leadership and professional excellence.</strong>
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>Recognizing that education should be accessible beyond the walls of a traditional classroom, South
            Eastern Arabic College adopts flexible and innovative learning models. Educational opportunities are
            offered wherever resources are available—whether in homes, community centers, or open public spaces. The
            effective use of modern technology, including digital platforms and online learning tools, further
            enhances access and reach. Personalized learning sessions are also provided to meet individual academic
            goals and learning needs.</strong>
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>Looking toward the future, South Eastern Arabic College is actively preparing to expand its
            face-to-face and blended learning programs on a global scale. While currently centered in Sri Lanka,
            plans are underway to make high-quality academic and spiritual instruction available </strong><strong>to
            learners worldwide, ensuring that students everywhere can benefit from our guidance and educational
            services.</strong>
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>Through dedication, sacrifice, and a forward-looking vision, South Eastern Arabic College strives to
            develop intellectually accomplished, ethically grounded, and socially responsible individuals—capable of
            making meaningful contributions to their communities and to the world at large.</strong>
    </p>
